Attribution notices for the vendored Apache Ossie schemas
=========================================================

This file is not this repository's own notice. It carries, verbatim, the
attribution notices that upstream distributes alongside the two Ossie schemas
vendored under `schemas/`, because Apache-2.0 section 4(d) requires them to
travel with the bytes rather than stay behind in the repository they came from.
The headings, and this paragraph, are the only text here that is ours; nothing
inside the quoted blocks has been altered.

There are two notices rather than one, and that is the point of quoting both.
The two schemas were taken from two upstream revisions, and the project changed
hands between them: the specification was donated to the Apache Software
Foundation and renamed from OSI to Ossie. The revision the 0.1.1 bytes come
from carries the pre-donation notice, naming Open Semantic Interchange. The
revision the 0.2.0.dev0 bytes come from carries the Apache one. Shipping only
the newer would drop the attribution the older bytes were published under, and
shipping only the older would misattribute the newer.

`specs.toml` records which file came from which revision, with a digest for
each.


